    "description": "Developed the infrastructure utilizing Terraform to transition Python-based models onPrem to the Cloud utilizing Amazon Web Services such as S3, ECR, Docker, Lambda, and SQS with the goal of providing more swift access to results \nDeveloped a multi-project pipeline utilizing Gitlab’s CI/CD triggering jobs in other pipelines while also streamlining dependency variables and incorporating Terraform Enterprise to deploy the project to AWS resulting in a speedy process of testing and deploying\nDeveloped a Lambda that generates temporary authorization tokens from AWS IAM Roles and established a Rest API using Spring Boot and Java that retrieves the generated tokens via HTTP requests.\nUtilized AngularJs framework and languages utilized in web development such as HTML and JavaScript to collaborate with a team towards the designing and deployment of a website that allows for employees transitioning between project groups to remove themselves from their previous ones\nBecame familiar and deployed serializers within a web-based mapping built upon the Django framework while also refactoring previously created code to eliminate present bugs in the Python-based API\nCreated portlets in HTML and JavaScript that utilized API calls to fetch repositories and project groups the employee is currently a part of and direct them to the websites in which they can remove themselves from their previous groups increasing the speed of transitioning between projects\nUtilized the Unity Engine and Microsoft’s C# to initialize the development of a virtual reality training experience for familiarization of vehicular parts for internal Claims representatives\nInitiated the development of a desktop learning product utilizing Articulate while considering the accessibility of the learning experience for employees who are not able to utilize Oculus equipment",
